---
import { cuts, shop, paymentSteps } from './model.mjs';
interface Props { kind: 'chain' | 'target' | 'payment' }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const number = kind === 'chain' ? 1 : kind === 'target' ? 2 : 4;
const title = kind === 'chain' ? 'Later files cannot bridge a gap' : kind === 'target' ? 'The stopping point changes every later fact' : 'Record the charge that already happened';
const events = [
  ['Order 103 commits', 'Pending · agreed total 29.00'],
  ['Mistaken price commits', 'P7 catalogue price → 2.20'],
  ['Payment 504 commits', '10.00 by card · 19.00 still due'],
];
---
<figure class="recovery-figure" data-kind={kind} aria-labelledby={`recovery-title-${kind}`}>
  <figcaption id={`recovery-title-${kind}`}><span class="figure-number">Figure {number}</span> {title}</figcaption>
  <div class="figure-box">
    {kind === 'chain' && <>
      <label class="option">Retained history <select aria-label="Retained history for figure 1" data-chain-option><option value="complete">Complete A → B → C</option><option value="missing">Interval B is missing</option></select></label>
      <p class="lane-label">Required dependencies, in order →</p>
      <ol class="chain" aria-label="Starting backup and required log intervals">
        <li><strong>Starting copy</strong><span>Base backup and the WAL needed to make it consistent</span><em>Available</em></li>
        <li><strong>History A</strong><span>Includes order 103</span><em>Reachable</em></li>
        <li data-interval-b><strong>History B</strong><span>Includes the price mistake</span><em data-chain-b data-live>Reachable</em></li>
        <li data-interval-c><strong>History C</strong><span>Includes payment 504</span><em data-chain-c data-live>Reachable</em></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="result" data-chain-result data-live>Latest covered point shown: end of C</p>
      <p class="explanation" data-chain-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The starting copy and every required interval are available. A supported restore can reach the shown points through C.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'target' && <>
      <label class="option">Restore to <select aria-label="Restore target for figure 2" data-cut-option>{cuts.map((cut, i) => <option value={i}>{cut.label}</option>)}</select></label>
      <div class="target-grid">
        <div><p class="lane-label">Original committed history →</p><ol class="events">{events.map(([event, detail], i) => <li data-event={i} class:list={{retained:i === 0}}><strong>{event}</strong><span>{detail}</span><em data-event-state data-live>{i === 0 ? 'Retained' : 'Omitted by this cut'}</em></li>)}</ol></div>
        <div><p class="lane-label">Recovered database</p><dl class="facts"><div><dt>P7 catalogue</dt><dd data-cut-price data-live>20.00</dd></div><div><dt>Order 103</dt><dd>Pending · 29.00</dd></div><div><dt>Payment 504</dt><dd data-cut-payment data-live>Absent</dd></div><div><dt>Recorded due</dt><dd data-cut-due data-live>29.00</dd></div></dl><p class="stock">Stock: {shop.stock}</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="provider"><strong>Provider · outside the restore</strong><span>Accepted 10.00 for order 103</span><code>{shop.operation}</code></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-cut-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">{cuts[0].explanation}</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'payment' && <>
      <label class="option">Provider lookup <select aria-label="Provider outcome for figure 4" data-payment-option><option value="accepted">Accepted · order and amount match</option><option value="unknown">Outcome unavailable</option><option value="mismatch">Order or amount disagrees</option></select></label>
      <p class="identity"><strong>Original operation</strong><code>{shop.operation}</code><span>Order 103 · payment 504 · 10.00 by card</span></p>
      <div class="payment-grid">
        <div class="payment-local"><p class="lane-label">Restored database</p><strong data-local data-live>No payment 504</strong><span data-mapping data-live>No operation mapping</span></div>
        <div class="provider"><p class="lane-label">Independent provider evidence</p><strong data-provider data-live>Accepted · 10.00</strong><span>This history is not rewound</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="result" data-action data-live>External dispatch disabled</p>
      <div class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"><strong data-step-title>{paymentSteps[0].title}</strong><p data-step-text>{paymentSteps[0].text}</p></div>
      <div class="player" role="group" aria-label="Figure 4 controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 6</span><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
    </>}
  </div>
  <p class="caption">{kind === 'chain' ? 'A PostgreSQL-style base-and-WAL model. A, B and C are invented intervals, not file names or measured log positions. The picture shows dependency order, not elapsed time or equal file sizes.' : kind === 'target' ? 'Three cuts in one illustrative recovery branch. Order 103’s agreed P7 price stays 20.00; changing or restoring the catalogue does not reprice it. The provider’s known accepted result is assumed for this drawing.' : 'A controlled reconciliation after the source history is closed. This is a model, with a hypothetical queryable provider; it is not a trace of a real payment service. Changing the lookup changes where the procedure must stop.'}</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary>{kind === 'chain' ? <p>The starting copy needs its own consistency WAL. History A includes order 103; B includes the mistake; C includes payment 504. With every dependency present the pictured chain reaches C. Without B, this chain reaches A but cannot reach B or C even if C’s files exist.</p> : kind === 'target' ? <ul>{cuts.map(cut => <li><strong>{cut.label}:</strong> P7 {cut.price}; payment 504 {cut.payment.toLowerCase()}; recorded due {cut.due}. {cut.explanation}</li>)}</ul> : <><ol>{paymentSteps.map(step => <li><strong>{step.title}.</strong> {step.text}</li>)}</ol><p>An unavailable provider result or mismatching order/amount stops before a payment is inserted. No branch creates a new charge.</p></>}</details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  import { cuts, paymentState, paymentSteps } from './model.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.recovery-figure').forEach(root => {
    const put = (selector: string, text: string) => { const element = root.querySelector(selector); if (element) element.textContent = text; };
    if (root.dataset.kind === 'chain') {
      const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-chain-option]')!;
      const draw = () => {
        const missing = select.value === 'missing';
        root.querySelector('[data-interval-b]')!.classList.toggle('missing', missing);
        root.querySelector('[data-interval-c]')!.classList.toggle('blocked', missing);
        put('[data-chain-b]', missing ? 'Missing' : 'Reachable');
        put('[data-chain-c]', missing ? 'Files present; unreachable' : 'Reachable');
        put('[data-chain-result]', missing ? 'Latest covered point shown: end of A' : 'Latest covered point shown: end of C');
        put('[data-chain-explanation]', missing ? 'This chain cannot cross the missing interval B. Keeping C does not repair the gap. A different complete backup path might reach later; this one cannot.' : 'The starting copy and every required interval are available. A supported restore can reach the shown points through C.');
      };
      select.addEventListener('change', draw); draw();
    }
    if (root.dataset.kind === 'target') {
      const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cut-option]')!;
      const draw = () => {
        const cut = cuts[Number(select.value)];
        root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-event]').forEach((element, i) => {
          element.classList.toggle('retained', i < cut.retained);
          element.querySelector('[data-event-state]')!.textContent = i < cut.retained ? 'Retained' : 'Omitted by this cut';
        });
        put('[data-cut-price]', cut.price); put('[data-cut-payment]', cut.payment); put('[data-cut-due]', cut.due); put('[data-cut-explanation]', cut.explanation);
      };
      select.addEventListener('change', draw); draw();
    }
    if (root.dataset.kind === 'payment') {
      const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-payment-option]')!;
      const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => select.value === 'accepted' ? paymentSteps.length : 3,
        draw: (step: number) => {
          const state = paymentState(step, select.value);
          put('[data-local]', state.local); put('[data-mapping]', state.mapping); put('[data-action]', state.action); put('[data-step-title]', state.title); put('[data-step-text]', state.text);
          put('[data-provider]', select.value === 'accepted' ? 'Accepted · 10.00' : select.value === 'unknown' ? 'Outcome unavailable' : 'Payload disagrees');
        }
      });
      select.addEventListener('change', player.render);
    }
  });
</script>
<style>
.recovery-figure { margin: 2rem 0; }
figcaption { font: 1.2rem/1.4 var(--font-serif); margin-bottom: .6rem; }
.figure-number { font: .7rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-right: .5rem; white-space: nowrap; }
.figure-box { padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background: var(--color-surface-alt); font: .88rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
.option { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .5rem; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
select { max-width: 100%; min-width: 0; padding: .45rem; font: inherit; background: var(--color-surface); color: var(--color-text); border: 1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); border-radius: .2rem; }
.lane-label { font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 .65rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
.chain { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: .7rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
.chain li, .events li { position: relative; padding: .65rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); background: var(--color-surface); margin: 0; }
.chain li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '→'; position: absolute; right: -.65rem; top: 42%; font-weight: bold; }
.chain strong, .chain span, .chain em, .events strong, .events span, .events em { display: block; }
.chain span { margin: .4rem 0; font-size: .8rem; }
.chain em, .events em { font-style: normal; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--color-accent-strong); }
.chain li.missing { border-style: dashed; border-width: 2px; }
.chain li.blocked em, .chain li.missing em { color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 700; }
.target-grid, .payment-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
.events { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: .7rem; }
.events li { border-style: dashed; }
.events li.retained { border-style: solid; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); }
.events span { font-size: .8rem; margin: .2rem 0; }
.facts { margin: 0; }
.facts div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding: .6rem 0; }
.facts dt { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
.facts dd { margin: 0; font-weight: 600; text-align: right; }
.stock { font-size: .8rem; margin: .7rem 0; }
.provider, .payment-local { display: grid; align-content: start; gap: .3rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); padding: .75rem; background: var(--color-surface); }
.target-grid + .provider { margin-top: 1rem; border-style: double; border-width: 3px; }
.provider code, .identity code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: transparent; padding: 0; }
.provider span, .payment-local span { font-size: .8rem; }
.identity { display: grid; gap: .25rem; padding-bottom: .75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); }
.result { font-weight: 600; margin: 1rem 0 .7rem; }
.explanation { min-height: 5rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); padding-left: .8rem; margin: 0; }
.explanation p { margin: .4rem 0 0; }
.player { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .45rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: .75rem; }
button { padding: .45rem .7rem; font: inherit; color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); border-radius: .2rem; cursor: pointer; }
button[aria-disabled='true'] { color: var(--color-text-secondary); border-style: dashed; cursor: default; }
button:focus-visible, select:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset: 3px; }
[data-step] { font: .8rem var(--font-mono); margin-left: auto; }
[data-hold] { width: 100%; height: 3px; background: var(--color-rule); }
[data-hold] span { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--color-accent); width: 0; }
.caption { color: var(--color-text-secondary); font: .8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); margin: .6rem 0; }
details { font: .85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--color-accent); }
details p, details ol, details ul { margin: .7rem 0; }
@media(max-width: 600px) { .chain { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; } .chain li:not(:last-child)::after { content: '↓'; right: 48%; top: auto; bottom: -1rem; } .target-grid, .payment-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .explanation { min-height: 0; } }
@media(max-width: 390px) { .figure-box { padding: .75rem; } .chain { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; } .chain li:not(:last-child)::after, .chain li:nth-child(2)::after, .chain li:nth-child(3)::after { content: '↓'; right: 48%; top: auto; bottom: -1rem; } }
@media(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { [data-hold] span { transition: none !important; } }
</style>
